{:theorem
 {:id :theorem,
  :statement
  "Under conjugation by the T gate $T = \\text{diag}(1, e^{i\\pi/4})$: $T I T^\\dagger = I$, $T Z T^\\dagger = Z$, $T X T^\\dagger = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(X + Y)$, $T Y T^\\dagger = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(Y - X)$.",
  :content-hash "df5b280d09142e8e"},
 :obligations [],
 :archived-nodes {},
 :external-refs {},
 :nodes
 {:1-t3a001
  {:statement
   "The T gate is defined as $T = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & e^{i\\pi/4} \\end{pmatrix} = \\text{diag}(1, \\omega)$ where $\\omega = e^{i\\pi/4} = \\frac{1+i}{\\sqrt{2}}$. Note $T^\\dagger = \\text{diag}(1, \\omega^*)$ where $\\omega^* = e^{-i\\pi/4}$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "7f8250c990251162",
   :display-order 1,
   :type :definition,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :definition-expansion,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-t3a001,
